&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="what-every-module-is-held-to"&gt;What every module is held to&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="what-every-module-is-held-to"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#what-every-module-is-held-to" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;CGO_ENABLED=0&lt;/code&gt;: no cgo, and no shelling out to a command-line tool in place
of a library.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-compiled for amd64, arm64, riscv64, loong64, ppc64le and s390x — the
last big-endian, which keeps every wire encoding honest — and, where it
applies, &lt;code&gt;js/wasm&lt;/code&gt;. Twelve of the nineteen do all six today, two are
browser applications, and the other five are listed in &lt;a href="https://go-widgets.github.io/docs/0.2/status/#what-ci-does-not-cover-yet"&gt;Status&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A statement-coverage gate in CI: 100% in eighteen of the nineteen. Where a
file cannot run in a test (a browser loop, a native run loop), the module
says which file is left out and why. See &lt;a href="https://go-widgets.github.io/docs/0.2/status/"&gt;Status&lt;/a&gt;
for the exceptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BSD-3-Clause.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>